  "notes": [
   "Microsoft Flight Simulator 2024 runs on Highball's native arm64 preview engine, which this recipe asks for, and the Intel engines cannot start it. The engine needs macOS 26.5 or later. It was tested on a Mac with 32 GB of memory, where the game used 25 to 27 GB. The first start takes about seven minutes to the start screen and four more from Start to the cockpit, and later starts reuse the shader and code caches. On a base M4 in daylight, expect 22 to 25 fps parked and 19 to 21 on the take-off roll at the Medium preset with FSR Balanced. Turn Motion Blur off in the graphics settings."
  ],
  "knownIssues": [
   {
