    "fix": "this recipe's engine r6 starts it, and Highball offers the move when you press Play"
   },
   {
    "symptom": "A Honeycomb Bravo throttle quadrant shows up as a gamepad (Controller_1) and its levers move the menus, or the Alpha yoke does not show up at all",
    "cause": "Wine's controller driver counted the Bravo, six levers and dozens of switches, as a gamepad when it read it through SDL, and Apple's game controller layer hid the Alpha",
    "fix": "this recipe's Flight controls as on Windows tweak reads Honeycomb devices directly, as Windows does; from Highball 0.10.23, Play applies it to environments set up before"
   },
   {
    "symptom": "On the Intel engines the game refuses to start with 'Your graphics card does not support Shader Model 6.7', or quits during its first loading screen",
    "cause": "D3DMetal 3 and the first D3DMetal 4 betas report Shader Model 6.6, and past that check the game stops during its first load under Rosetta",
    "fix": "this recipe asks for the native arm64 preview engine, which Play offers for this game"
   },
   {
    "symptom": "A short freeze of one to two seconds a few times a flight, more in daylight",
    "cause": "Metal stopping on lossless-compressed images the game copies every frame",
    "fix": "this recipe sets HB_MVK_NO_LOSSLESS=1 on the environment, which removes most of them, and one flight in four still shows two in daylight"
   },
   {
    "symptom": "About one start in sixteen to forty ends in a crash during the world load",
    "cause": "under study (memory corruption during the load)",
    "fix": "none yet, start again"
   },
   {
    "symptom": "About seven minutes to the start screen and four more from Start to the cockpit",
    "cause": "the emulator translating the game's code, the shader preparation and the game unpacking its packages on one thread",
    "fix": "none, later starts reuse the shader and code caches"
   },
   {
