    "valueType": "REG_SZ",
    "data": "n,b",
    "platforms": [
     "mac"
    ]
   }
  ],
  "notes": [
   "Optional, never applied by Play: puts the DXVK-MacOS 3.1 Direct3D 9 (the engine's d9vk-modern directory) beside RRRE64.exe with a per-program override, so this game alone runs on it while every other game keeps the default layer. It rendered the game, practice and races with AI, for one reporter on an M3 whose sessions froze with VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST on the default layer (highball-db#60); when the withdrawn r4 engine put the same layer on every launch's path, another reporter got RaceRoom in grayscale and a third had Five Nights at Freddy's freeze, so it is offered under Advanced rather than applied. On the maintainer's M1 Pro the same DLL runs Five Nights at Freddy's without a freeze (2026-09-18). RaceRoom itself is not installed here (74 GB)."
  ],
  "knownIssues": [
   {
    "symptom": "Pre-race screen freezes after the track loads, VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST in the Direct3D 9 log (default layer)",
    "cause": "reported: the DXVK-Kegworks 1.10.4 Direct3D 9 loses the Metal device on this game",
    "fix": "apply this optional fix under Advanced on the game's page; if the picture turns grayscale, remove the copied d3d9.dll next to RRRE64.exe and the override, both reported outcomes exist"
   },
   {
    "symptom": "Applying this fix changes nothing on a DXVK launch",
    "cause": "measured 2026-09-20 on Half-Life 2 with +loaddll: on a DXVK launch the engine's own Direct3D 9 overlay is found before the copy beside the game's executable (the launch's WINEDLLOVERRIDES outranks the per-program registry entry), so the newer layer never loads; it loads on a wined3d launch",
    "fix": "none shipped yet; a per-program layer choice is planned (Highball plan item 14). Setting this game's mode to Wine's own Direct3D makes the copy the Direct3D 9 in use, untested on RaceRoom"
   }
  ],
  "verified": null,
  "source": "recipes/games/raceroom-racing-experience.json"
 },
 {
  "id": "red-dead-redemption-2",
  "title": "Red Dead Redemption 2",
  "steam": 1174180,
  "optIn": false,
  "steps": [
   {
    "type": "registry",
    "key": "HKCU\\Software\\Wine\\AppDefaults\\RDR2.exe\\DllOverrides",
    "name": "vulkan-1",
    "valueType": "REG_SZ",
    "data": "native,builtin",
    "platforms": [
     "mac"
    ]
   }
  ],
  "notes": [
   "Asks for the Wine 11 engine r15 or newer since 2026-10-03 (was r7). On r11 to r14 the Rockstar Games Launcher installer stops at once, and an environment already on an older revision is not moved on its own, so raising the pin makes Play offer the newest revision to those environments. Everything installed stays.",
   "Needs engine x64-crossover26.3-r6 or later (the recipe asks for r7, which carries the same MoltenVK plus the NVAPI stub other games need): its MoltenVK accepts the linear-tiled 3D, mipmapped and array images the game creates. On every earlier engine the game exits at 98 per cent of its first load.",
   "Install the Rockstar Games Launcher through Highball first (Add games, Rockstar) rather than letting Steam's first run install it: on engines r11 to r14 Steam's installer stops at once with 'make sure all instances of the Rockstar Games Launcher have been closed' (fixed in r15), and on r7 the launcher installed through Highball initialised Steam and started the game on an M4 (2026-10-02).",
   "Leave the game on its own Vulkan renderer (the default). The graphics mode setting applies to the Rockstar launcher, which needs DXMT, not to the game.",
   "Tested at 1280x720 windowed, set in Documents/Rockstar Games/Red Dead Redemption 2/Settings/system.xml (<screenWidth>, <screenHeight>, <windowed value=\"1\" />) after the first run writes the file. About 34 fps in the prologue snow on an M1 Pro.",
   "The first key after the game window regains focus is ignored. Press it again.",
   "On a 16 GB Mac the game is memory-bound: its footprint passes 13 GB in the prologue and macOS swaps, so the frame rate decays over a minute of play. In Documents/Rockstar Games/Red Dead Redemption 2/Settings/system.xml, vSync 0 and fsr2Index 2 (FSR 2 balanced) keep the menus and cutscenes smoother and halve the GPU time there; they do not remove the memory wall. 24 GB or more removes it.",
   "Epic copy: Highball 0.9.12 or later starts it through a stand-in for Epic's launcher so the Rockstar launcher accepts the entitlement. If the game then stops with Error 18 (its Vulkan layer missing), copy vulkan-1.dll from Program Files/Rockstar Games/Social Club next to RDR2.exe in the game folder; the per-program override above makes the game use it. Reported on an M5 Max on engine r8, main menu reached at 1080p ultra (highball#93)."
  ],
  "knownIssues": [
   {
    "symptom": "On engines before r6: loads to about 98 per cent, opens a window and exits without a frame (Vulkan), or crashes about 30 seconds in with DirectX 12 selected in system.xml.",
    "cause": "MoltenVK 1.4.1 refuses linear-tiled 3D, mipmapped and array images (fixed in r6's MoltenVK). D3DMetal answers a D3D12 call the game needs with 'Not implemented' (not fixable here).",
    "fix": "use engine x64-crossover26.3-r6 or later and leave the game on its default Vulkan renderer."
   },
   {
    "symptom": "One vertex shader fails to compile to Metal (gl_CullDistance emitted into an undeclared struct member) and the driver logs many bytes_per_row assertions during loading.",
    "cause": "SPIRV-Cross's Metal output for cull distance, and the row pitch of the game's linear 2D textures.",
    "fix": "none needed so far: nothing visibly missing in the prologue. Recorded so a texture glitch later has a lead."
   },
   {
    "symptom": "On engines r11 to r14 the Rockstar Games Launcher installer stops right after it starts with 'make sure all instances of the Rockstar Games Launcher have been closed' and the launcher is never installed.",
    "cause": "a Highball engine patch from r11 returned a heap pointer from GetLastError() after the first display call of a process; the installer reads it right after it measures the display.",
    "fix": "engine x64-crossover26.3-r15 (Highball 0.10.3). r7, the revision this recipe names, does not have the fault."
   }
  ],
  "verified": {
   "date": "2026-10-02",
   "engine": "x64-crossover26.3-r15",
   "chip": "Apple M4"
  },
  "source": "recipes/games/red-dead-redemption-2.json"
 },
 {
  "id": "the-last-caretaker",
  "title": "The Last Caretaker",
  "steam": 1783560,
  "optIn": false,
  "steps": [
   {
    "type": "registry",
    "key": "HKCU\\Software\\Wine\\AppDefaults\\VoyageSteam-Win64-Shipping.exe\\DllOverrides",
    "name": "mfplat",
    "valueType": "REG_SZ",
    "data": "",
    "platforms": [
     "mac"
    ]
   }
  ],
  "notes": [
   "The menu plays a 4K 60 fps video (Content/Movies/Menubgvideo4k60.mp4) through Windows Media Foundation. Under Wine the decoded frames reach D3DMetal as a texture it has no Metal format for: Metal refuses the descriptor (invalid pixelFormat 0), the thread that asked dies, and the game's main thread then waits on it forever, so the window stays black at idle GPU. With Media Foundation's platform library disabled for the game's executable only, the media player fails to open the file, the menu comes up without its background video, and the game plays. Nothing else in the environment changes."
  ],
  "knownIssues": [],
  "verified": {
   "date": "2026-09-19",
   "engine": "x64-sikarugir10.0_6-r5",
   "chip": "Apple M1 Pro"
  },
  "source": "recipes/games/the-last-caretaker.json"
 },
 {
  "id": "warframe",
  "title": "Warframe",
  "steam": 230410,
  "optIn": false,
  "steps": [
   {
    "type": "registry",
    "key": "HKCU\\Software\\Wine\\AppDefaults\\Launcher.exe\\DllOverrides",
    "name": "dwrite",
    "valueType": "REG_SZ",
    "data": "",
    "platforms": [
     "mac"
    ]
   }
  ],
  "notes": [
   "Warframe's Steam entry starts Tools\\Launcher.exe, an updater with an embedded browser, and that browser paints nothing under this engine's DirectWrite (a black window with no buttons). The override above disables DirectWrite for Launcher.exe alone, so the launcher draws with GDI text, shows its EULA and Play button, and updates the game. The game keeps DirectWrite. Use DXMT for the game; DXVK runs it too but at about half the frame rate. The same per-executable override was described by leontov-eng on Sikarugir issue #255 on 2026-08-24; Highball ships it as data so nobody has to find winecfg."
  ],
  "knownIssues": [
   {
    "symptom": "The Warframe launcher window is black; the game never updates or starts",
    "cause": "the launcher's embedded browser renders through DirectWrite, which paints nothing in this Wine (Sikarugir #255 has the same symptom for other CEF launchers)",
    "fix": "the registry step in this recipe, verified 2026-09-04: the launcher showed its EULA, updated the game and started it"
   },
   {
    "symptom": "'Login with Steam' fails and a bind-or-create dialog appears",
    "cause": "the Steam account has no Warframe account linked yet; this is the game's own flow, not an engine problem",
    "fix": "choose Create New or Bind Existing in that dialog"
   }
  ],
  "verified": {
   "date": "2026-09-04",
   "engine": "x64-sikarugir10.0_6-r1",
   "chip": "Apple M1 Pro"
  },
  "source": "recipes/games/warframe.json"
 }
]
''';
